0..77 Comment "// This source ports the parts of Ahman and Bauer\'s oracle sheaves that gandr"
78..88 Comment "// checks."
89..91 Comment "//"
92..170 Comment "// The port tests whether gandr states an intensional sheaf. A tree keeps each"
171..249 Comment "// query that it asks, and no truncation hides an answer. Membership at a leaf"
250..314 Comment "// is a tree of paths, so a proof of it records the queries too."
315..317 Comment "//"
318..395 Comment "// The parameters `s` and `p` of each family are a container: queries and the"
396..475 Comment "// answers to each. The oracle modality of a container is its trees, their bind"
476..555 Comment "// and their fold. A sheaf is an algebra whose two equations are `Path` fields."
556..558 Comment "//"
559..574 Comment "// - see: #4728"
575..659 Comment "// - see: `../../pathological/effects/oracle-sheaves.gandr` — where the port stops"
660..712 Comment "// - cites: [Ahman-2026-sheaves_oracle_computations]"
713..715 Comment "//"
716..845 Comment "// [Ahman-2026-sheaves_oracle_computations]: https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.22135v2 \"Ahman and Bauer, Sheaves as Oracle Computations\""
